# scripts/usage-report/.env.example — template for the standalone usage/cost-report CLI (epic #3383).
#
# THIS FILE IS A TEMPLATE ONLY. NEVER commit a real .env — and note this template does NOT even live where
# the real file goes: usage-report.mjs reads its real secrets from OUTSIDE this repo entirely, at
#   ~/.we-usage-report/.env
# (your home directory, resolved via `os.homedir()` — see scripts/lib/usage-report-secret-paths.mjs). Copy
# this template THERE, not to scripts/usage-report/.env. See ./README.md for the full reasoning, the exact
# path, and a stronger macOS-Keychain-backed alternative to this plain file.
#
# THIS KEY MUST NEVER BE EXPORTED into any shell that also runs the driver/dispatch pipeline
# (deliver-item-wrapper.mjs, fix-dispatch-wrapper.mjs, ci-heal-dispatch-wrapper.mjs,
# minimal-context-provider.mjs, dispatch-lane-io.mjs — every one of them spreads `{...process.env, ...}`
# wholesale into every dispatched agent it spawns, Claude AND Codex, today). Run this tool from its own
# one-off shell invocation only — never source this file into your interactive session's long-lived shell,
# and never add it to a shell profile (.zshrc/.bashrc) that a dispatch-spawning process might inherit from.

# ── Anthropic Admin API key. Requires an organization with the admin role (unavailable for individual
#    accounts) — Console → Settings → Organization → Admin API keys. Starts with `sk-ant-admin...`. ──
ANTHROPIC_ADMIN_KEY=

# ── OpenAI Admin API key. Requires an "Owner" role on the organization — platform.openai.com → Settings →
#    Organization → Admin keys ("API keys" are NOT sufficient; only an Admin key can read usage/costs). ──
OPENAI_ADMIN_KEY=
